    /**
     * Publish a new immutable `config` version for an existing scorer. Use this whenever the scoring rules change (add/remove categorical options, tweak numeric bounds or passing rules, change boolean polarity or labels). Existing trace reviews keep their snapshot of the previous version, so historical scores remain stable. The `config` shape must match the scorer's `kind`. Each call increments `current_version` by one. Pass `base_version` (the version number you observed before bumping) for optimistic concurrency — the request returns 409 if another writer already advanced the scorer. Optional `name` and `description` updates are saved atomically with the version. For a composite scorer, also provide the full `composition`, even when only the output rules change. Its formula and input version UUIDs are pinned to the new version; updating a source scorer never updates dependent composites automatically. When available, validate the proposed composition with `llma-score-definition-validate` before saving. Numeric composites do not accept `step`.
     *
     * @mcpTool llma-score-definition-new-version
     *
     * @requiredScopes llm_analytics:write
     */
